what is thread ?
in this os we have process and inside the process we have thread and every thread have independent stack (LIFO) but share the same 
memory which is heap.
->one process will have multiple thread 
Smallest sequence of instructions that are execute by cpu independently that are called thread 


===============================================================================================================
So suppose that there are two process are running so there memory will be independed they will not have the same memory 
====================================
When a Process is created it start with 1 thread and that initial thread know as 'main thread' and from that we can create multiple threads to perform task concurrently. 
So one process have multiple thread 



How much memory does process get? 
answer:- While creating the process "java MainClassName" command a new JVM instance will get created and we can tell how much memory need to be allocated . 

java-Xm256m-Xmx2g MainClassName
-Xms<size>:
This will set the intial heap size,above i allocated 256mb. It will start with 256mb of memory.
-Xmx<size>:
This will set the maximum heap size,above i allocated 2gb. It will not exceed more than 2gb.
if tries to allocate more memory "outofMemoryError"will occur

how the program run 
1.Create a process 
2.jvm instance created 



So the heap Memory 
Code segment Data Segment are shared to the every thread suppose that there are three thread then that three thread will share this but the every thread have there individual Register,stack,counter,thread1 so every thread have this 


1.Code segment:- 
Contains the complied BYTECODE i.e machine code of the java program 
It's read only 
All thread with the same process share the same code segment 
2.Data segment 
Contains the GLOBAL and STATIC variables. 
All thread within the same process,share the same data segment.
Threads can read and modify the same data. 
Synchronization is required between multiple threads. 
Heap:- 
objects are created on the heap memory with the new keyword
Heap is shared among all the threads of the same process 
Threads can read and modify the heap data. 
Synchronization is required between multiple threads.

Stack: 
Each thread has it's own stack;
It manages,method calls,local variable 
Register: 
When jit just-in-time compiles the bytecode into native machine codes its uses registers to 
optimized the generated machine code 
Also helps in context switching between threads 
Each thread has it's own Register
Counter that is Program counter: 
->Also known as program counter it point to the instructions which is getting executed 
->Increments its counter after succesfully  execution of the instructions 

All these are managed by jvm 

So like this when suppose that we have mutliple task like this so we are runnign the program  and then 50 cpu executed then it will context switch and then it will pick the again other t2 thread and then it will take the another task 

so suppose that if you have multiple cpu like 
cpu1 and cpu2 and cpu3 
then on that time 
t1 pick by cpu1 and t2 pick by cpu2 then on this time called parralllism 

Definition of Multithreading:- 
Allows a program to perform multiple task or multiple operation simultaneously 
Multiple threads share the same resources such as a memory  space but still can perform task independently 
Benefits :- 
Improved performance by task parallelism
Responsivness
Resource sharing 
Challeng:
Concurrency issues by deadlock data inconsistency etc 
synchornized overhead.
testing and dubbing is diffuclt



Multitasking vs multithread
